{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967689-100-ways-to-make-a-zombie-ravenant-ghoul","id":967689,"title":"100 ways to make a Zombie/Ravenant/Ghoul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-11T19:56:15-07:00","id":967689,"title":"100 ways to make a Zombie/Ravenant/Ghoul","content":"So..i been reading too much about zombies (voodoo, frankenstein etc...) and i was wondering, how would you make one in every game line. the tricks here are different Kinds of Zombies.<br /> One: Rottening cadaver a la romero<br /> two: frankenstein kind of creature (patched from different body parts and that's slowly gaining awareness)<br /> three: voodoo zombie slave<br /> fourth: Human body posessed or inhabited by its former spirit or by a spiritual being. regaining memories and consciousness<br /> <br /> one extra catch...Lets say that you explain how a garou (Uktena Theurge) manages to bring a human back to life as an Aberration against Gaia, i mean..Zombie. The catch is that now you must also explain how to bring a Garou and a Kinfolk back as a zombie. In the case of a mage, you must explain how would you resurrect a mage and an adept and so on...the idea is to see how different factions would &quot;Replace a Lightbulb&quot; (just like in the joke...If the joke was a loved one dead carcass)<br /> <br /> <br /> also, by Ghoul i dont mean Vampire servant.. i mean more of a undead creature that feeds on human flesh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 09-12-2016, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T23:33:15-07:00","id":967795,"title":"","content":"Mage time.<br /> ..oh dear, where to begin.<br /> <br /> First off, independant of Zombie *type* you have several options when it comes to actually having something like intelligence in the Zombie:<br /> <br /> - Use Spirit 5 along with potentially hazardous literal soulsearching to bring somebody's soul back from the Lower Umbra. For sure an interesting experience for the Wraith - and of course it only works as long as they became a Wraith to begin with. If the target in question is a Mage's soul, probably add Prime 5 to tie their Avatar back into that body, unless you want them to be essentially a non-Mage on return. No special steps needed for a sorceror/acolyte/whatev. Treat as normal human.<br /> - Make it a host for an existing Umbral spirit through bargaining with a spirit, then using Spirit 4.<br /> - Force a spirit to enter the undead host with Spirit 4.<br /> - Create a literal Spirit from scratch with Spirit 5 inside it.<br /> - Create a Mind from scratch with Mind 5 to make a new intelligence.<br /> - Killing somebody but not letting them escape the body: Mind 5+Life 4 according to HDYDT.<br /> - Semi-intelligence-exception: Have the creature act purely on mechanical instinct, forgoing Spirit and Mind and using Life. Yes, life - you're creating an undead at this point that is in the same weird Life/Matter hybrid state as a vampire, but purely acting on instinct. Without Mind though, it will never develop any intelligence.<br /> <br /> There we go. Now for the zombie body types:<br /> * Cadaver? Prime 2, Life 2. If the cadaver already is in a state of rot, replace Life 2 with Matter 2. If wanting to prevent rot for a long time, add Entropy 3.<br /> * Frankenstein: Mend the pieces through Life 4, then proceed as with 'Cadaver'. Preventing rot forever requires a powerful Entropy effect. Alternatively, use Quintessence, Prime 3 and Life 4 to return the body to actual life.<br /> * Voodoo zombie slave is a combination of the Cadaver body type, and the 'Killing somebody..' soul type.<br /> * Human body with former soul' is a combination of the 'Soulsearching Spirit 5' intelligence variant, combined with Cadaver and using the mentioned Quintessence, Prime 3, Life 4 effect to make the body alive again. Alternatively use the Frankenstein Entropy effect to prevent rot.<br /> <br /> The 'eating human flesh' part can be reasoned by either having that as part of the instinct from the 'Semi-intelligence-exception' entry above, *or* imbueing the zombie with an inherent Life 3/Prime 4 ability which causes eaten flesh to become Quintessence which fuels the Entropy 3 effect that prevents the body rot (see: iZombie series where eating the flesh prevents exactly that.)<br /> <br /> <br /> P.s. 7 ways of adding intelligence, times 4 different body types...you just got 28 ways of making a Zombie/Revenant/Ghoul!<br /> 72 to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> -","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-12-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:38:03-07:00","id":968272,"title":"","content":"So..How to make a zombie in Werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T18:39:43-07:00","id":968293,"title":"","content":"Easy enough. You create a fomori with Autonomy 1. It is effectively under the complete control of its resident Bane and, because most Banes do not care about personal hygiene, it will stink worse than any rotting corpse. It will also have 45 Power Points, which will make it the equivalent of a walking cruise missile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T18:57:16-07:00","id":968303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967689-100-ways-to-make-a-zombie-ravenant-ghoul?p=968293#post968293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy enough. You create a fomori with Autonomy 1. It is effectively under the complete control of its resident Bane and, because most Banes do not care about personal hygiene, it will stink worse than any rotting corpse. It will also have 45 Power Points, which will make it the equivalent of a walking cruise missile.</div> </div> </div> </div>and how you turn a garou/kinfolk into a zombie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:14:25-07:00","id":968309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967689-100-ways-to-make-a-zombie-ravenant-ghoul?p=968303#post968303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and how you turn a garou/kinfolk into a zombie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you're accepting that as a way, then do the same thing to a Garou/Kinfolk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would actually say that having a Death Spirit use the Possession Charm would be a little closer to what you are thinking of. It is effectibely the same thing, but the power behind it should color the Possession. And hey, it might not even be Wyrm Tainted (possibly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:10:14-07:00","id":968330,"title":"","content":"A fomori Garou is a bit unlikely, they can fight back, but a Kinfolk fomori is a possibility, though they generally belong to cultures that have exorcist traditions (whether they use Appalachian witchcraft, Cherokee shamanism, or Georgia hoo-doo).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:22:55-07:00","id":968334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967689-100-ways-to-make-a-zombie-ravenant-ghoul?p=968330#post968330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fomori Garou is a bit unlikely, they can fight back, but a Kinfolk fomori is a possibility, though they generally belong to cultures that have exorcist traditions (whether they use Appalachian witchcraft, Cherokee shamanism, or Georgia hoo-doo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessed Garou can and do happen. having any sort of zombie-Garou is unlikely. And actually, come to think of it the first Fomori book had Howling Shamblers, which is at least close to what the OP was looking for.<br /> <br /> And since there are plenty of Gaian Death Spirits, a Possessed Garou could very well be a Gorgon as opposed to a Fomori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:06:27-07:00","id":968349,"title":"","content":"A Wyld spirit will not possess a sapient entity. Even a Garou is too filled with the Weaver and the Wyrm for a Wyld spirit to tolerate. Of course, an Autonomy 1 Drone could be a zombie as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:57:47-07:00","id":968364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967689-100-ways-to-make-a-zombie-ravenant-ghoul?p=968349#post968349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Wyld spirit will not possess a sapient entity. Even a Garou is too filled with the Weaver and the Wyrm for a Wyld spirit to tolerate. Of course, an Autonomy 1 Drone could be a zombie as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gorgon is slightly the wrong term. I'm not talking about Wyld Spirits, I'm talking about Gaian Death Spirits. There is a difference. And this question (pertaining to Werewolf at least) is very much outside of the realm of what would &quot;normally&quot; happen. I can envision a few different circumstances where such an agreement could be come to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T04:55:12-07:00","id":968455,"title":"","content":"Um... If you're just looking for &quot;zombie garou&quot; for thematic purposes, I recommend Howling Shamblers (found in any Book of the Wyrm). It's a fomori that happens when a bane called a Howling Insanity possesses a Garou, resulting in a fomori that goes full zombie mode after being killed.<br /> <br /> I would venture that the Werewolf books probably only scratch the surface of the spirit world and Garou mysticism. I could easily see a wayward (either tainted, ronin, heretical, or a victim of the Twisted Ubringing flaw) Garou attempting to summon a dead ally's spirit and bind it back into their body using either existing Rites or trying to create their own. That could easily result in anything from a zombie to a makeshift Risen. A Silent Strider (with their ties to the Dark Umbra) or an Uktena (with their penchant for hedgemagic) would be the most likely to get to that point &quot;successfully&quot;.... but again, I could easily see a ronin cub who managed to get their hands on Summoning and Binding going for it as well. Keep in mind that the cycle of life and death is considered a natural part of Gaia, and bucking against it would be pretty severe religious heresy to the vast sweeping majority of Garou, and might be worthy of a death sentence in many Elders' eyes. (Or 2 hours in time-out with no videogames in W20... I haven't re-read enough fluff to know just how dancing/hand-holding/PC the Garou Nation has been rewritten to be)<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't be shocked if there was an existing (albeit not written that I'm aware of) bane that could possess or be bound into a dead body. Considering Psychomachae and Blood spirits are the only two that can possess and maintain control of Vampires, that might be a starting point for considering the types of spirits that could animate a corpse. (Also, at least one book mentions Fomori hosts can be anything from humans to animals to inanimate objects, but in later books I've only seen 'humans' or 'humans and animals' listed)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:23:09-07:00","id":968476,"title":"","content":"Actually, there are a few Banes that can possess dead bodies (there is an example in one of the books of the possession of a bag full of drowned kittens), so it is possible. It is just that most Banes prefer living hosts because the host brings something to the union. Of course, if you want Banes reanimation corpses, the old B zombie movies that deal with reanimation of the dead with chemical spills would be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:50:18-07:00","id":968489,"title":"","content":"Putrescent Servitude is a level 8 Thanatosis power that robs a mortal of free will and makes them extra tough; as well as making them corpse-like. It can also reanimate corpses. Considering it's level, only Baron Samedi or Samedi who engaged in Diablerie would have it.<br /> <br /> Books of Crafts Bata'a section has zombie creation as either Spirit 5 Life 4 to rip apart and trap the soul in animated body, or Mind 4 Life 4 to trap the mind in their own rotting corpse and yank the mind around till it falls apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-14-2016, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T01:31:46-07:00","id":969089,"title":"","content":"A Marauder in Zombie Quiet...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T03:58:28-07:00","id":969805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967689-100-ways-to-make-a-zombie-ravenant-ghoul#post967689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One: Rottening cadaver a la romero</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: Use the Bone Path's level 2 or 3 abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> two: frankenstein kind of creature (patched from different body parts and that's slowly gaining awareness) </div> </div> </div>Vampire: VICISSITUDE VICISSITUDE VICISSITUDE<br /> Mage: VICISS- ahem. Life 5 to create a new form of life, with Mind 4-5 to give it the capacity for intelligence. Mind 4 version is kinda dumb and doesn't really learn well. This is for an actual parallel for Frankenstein's creation; he was creating a new life in truth, not just something made of corpses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> three: voodoo zombie slave </div> </div> </div>All lines: bury someone until they're suffering oxygen deprivation and susceptible to suggestion. Using lots of drugs may also help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> fourth: Human body posessed or inhabited by its former spirit or by a spiritual being. regaining memories and consciousness </div> </div> </div>Wraith: Risen are a thing.<br /> Vampire: The Bone Path of Necromancy has this as its level 5 power. Alternatively, the Thaumaturgy Path for summoning and binding spirits could be used to make a Fetish using the body as a host object.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also, by Ghoul i dont mean Vampire servant.. i mean more of a undead creature that feeds on human flesh </div> </div> </div>Vampire: Acquire Human. Acquire Nagaraja. Exsanguinate human. Have Nagaraja feed human their Vitae to reanimate the human as a new Nagaraja.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}